1
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:10,050
A cube has edges of length X squared centimetres.

2
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,970
Its volume is X squared, all cubed.

3
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:17,130
Is X squared, all cubed, equal to X to the 5, or X to the 6?

4
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:20,390
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:25,330
X squared, all cubed, is X squared, times X squared, times X squared.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,910
That is 2 plus 2 plus 2, which is 6.

7
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,890
So it is X to the 6.

8
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,840
Check with X equals 2.

9
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:34,850
2 squared is 4, and 4 cubed is 64.

10
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,350
2 to the 6 is also 64.

11
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:41,600
Remember: 3 to the 4, times 3 squared, is 3 to the 6.

12
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:46,160
And 5 to the 7, divided by 5 cubed, is 5 to the 4.

13
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:48,340
The same laws work with letters.

14
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:50,120
Multiply: add the indices.

15
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:51,620
Divide: subtract them.

16
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:54,970
A power of a power: multiply the indices.

17
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:55,670
Your turn.

18
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,710
Simplify Y to the 9, divided by Y to the 4.

19
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:02,010
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,620
Dividing, so subtract the indices.

21
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:05,770
9 minus 4 is 5.

22
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:08,230
The answer is Y to the 5.

23
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:12,000
Deal with the numbers and the letters separately.

24
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:16,390
3 A to the 4, times 5 A squared, is 15 A to the 6.

25
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:21,370
12 B to the 7, divided by 4 B cubed, is 3 B to the 4.

26
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:25,320
Only add terms with exactly the same letter and power.

27
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:28,640
6 W cubed plus 2 W cubed is 8 W cubed.

28
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,020
Here is the method.

29
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:33,820
Step 1: multiply or divide the numbers first.

30
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:41,930
Step 2: for each letter, multiplying adds the indices, dividing subtracts, and a power of a power multiplies.

31
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:47,710
Step 3: a bracket raised to a power: apply the power to everything inside.

32
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:51,520
Step 4: check by substituting a small number.

33
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:54,760
Simplify 4 P cubed Q, times 2 P Q to the 5.

34
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:56,860
The numbers: 4 times 2 is 8.

35
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:59,120
P cubed times P is P to the 4.

36
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:02,150
Q times Q to the 5 is Q to the 6.

37
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:04,720
Simplify 3 K squared, all cubed.

38
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:05,930
Cube the 3: 27.

39
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,100
Cube K squared: K to the 6.

40
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:10,900
The answer is 27 K to the 6.

41
00:02:10,950 --> 00:02:11,620
Your turn.

42
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:13,920
Simplify 2 C cubed, all squared.

43
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:16,910
Pause and work it out.

44
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:19,450
Square the 2 too: 2 squared is 4.

45
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,920
C cubed, squared, is C to the 6.

46
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:24,550
The answer is 4 C to the 6.

47
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,420
Tom simplifies 2 Y to the 4, all cubed.

48
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:29,440
Which line is wrong?

49
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:30,540
Line 1 is wrong.

50
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:32,180
He forgot to cube the 2.

51
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:35,390
Everything inside the bracket is cubed.

52
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:39,730
2 cubed is 8, so the answer is 8 Y to the 12.

53
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,600
Index laws help in science.

54
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:49,790
If a balloon's radius doubles, its volume, which depends on R cubed, becomes 2 cubed, which is 8 times bigger.

55
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,120
One last question.

56
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:54,430
Can 6 W cubed plus 2 W squared be simplified?

57
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:57,820
Pause the video and choose.

58
00:02:57,870 --> 00:02:58,020
No.

59
00:02:58,070 --> 00:03:00,820
W cubed and W squared are not like terms.

60
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:03,210
So it cannot be simplified.

61
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:05,900
To remember: multiply, add the indices.

62
00:03:05,950 --> 00:03:07,070
Divide, subtract.

63
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,480
Power of a power, multiply.

64
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:12,810
Deal with numbers and letters separately.

65
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:16,720
A power on a bracket applies to everything inside.

66
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:19,220
Only like terms can be added.

67
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:24,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.3 on Camday.
